{"title":"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Mary is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/8/1183a12017e48198b3352789cc39b223b17945d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> older than Sally, and Sally is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/e/f4e4e5c6d549ce47918b94180cad5c1644d9ea88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> younger than Danielle. The sum of their ages is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e779a9083cd1b359e12c25db9e2041212b342250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23.2$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> years. How old will Mary be on her next birthday?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eee1c556b95313f37fadd39b7c3512c19e877a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } 7\\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } 8\\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 9\\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } 10\\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ }  11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"359\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be Mary's age, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be Sally's age, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be Danielle's age.  \n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/2062bbed8e774512dd737d41650c69fb557c009e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=.6d$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd5e43d8f7f22dbc3b89e9744106f53eaceaf34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1.2s=1.2(.6d)=.72d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />.  \n</p><p>The sum of their ages is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/7831ce6ee5cb61a758304674561b17074c3fd950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+s+d=.72d+.6d+d=2.32d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"278\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/8574bd0bb5886b1fa4a518774e1f18107f0c1bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.32d=23.2$\" width=\"97\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48f49c25bebad7fde170b47bef3a86c188ed2c0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The smallest positive integer more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/8070d1cc13cadf2851ceb409ed6ff56e58e67998.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so Mary will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/173e69f812089a74e97d9a865f84e29d9a977040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> on her next birthday.\n</p><p>~modified by anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A\">2006 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_A